            "ImageDescription": {
              "value": "<p>The Citroen 2 CV was an air-cooled front-engine, front-wheel-drive economy car, built from 1948-90. The very basic style featured a full width, canvas, roll back sunroof\nThe 1948 2CV type A got a 9hp 375cc flat twin, one stop light, ripple bonnet and only available in grey\n1951; lockable doors, Fourgonnette van introduced\n1954; side repeaters at the back and 12hp 425cc\n1957; rear window enlarged, bonnet got an aluminium strip\n1960 round turn signals, bonnet now 5 rib, 4x4 Sahara introduced\n1963; 30hp 602cc\n1965; suicide doors replaced with front hinged\n1966; third side window\n1970; rectangular headlights (except the base model Special) and new tail lights, 435cc and 602cc available\n1978; 35hp 652cc \n1982; front disc brakes\nIn 1987 Citroen introduced the replacement, the AX, this year saw the discontinuation of the Club. This left the Special as the only regular 2CV model, alongside the more fashion-orientated Dolly, Charleston and the other special editions.\n</p>\nIn 1988, production ended",
              "source": "commons-desc-page"
            },
